{
  "Exports appointments to an iCalendar file (RFC 5545) and imports them back, for use with other calendar applications. The scheduler can also be printed.": "",
  "`exportICalendar()` writes the appointments of the displayed days, or all appointments. A series is exported whole with its rule, so another calendar repeats it the same way.": "",
  "Importing a file": "",
  "`importICalendar(text)` reads the events and adds them in the same way as any new appointment: to the array, or through a data source's adapter.": "",
  "What is exported and imported": "",
  "iCalendar": "",
  "The appointment": "",
  "The appointment's key. An individually edited occurrence uses the key of its series. On import, the UID becomes the new appointment's key (with a data source, the adapter assigns the key).": "",
  "In the appointment's own zone (`fields.startTimeZone`, `endTimeZone`), otherwise the scheduler's `timeZone`, otherwise the browser's, with `TZID`. All-day appointments are written as dates (`VALUE=DATE`), with the end on the following day.": "",
  "The text and the description, escaped and folded at 75 octets as RFC 5545 requires.": "",
  "The series rule. An `UNTIL` in wall clock time is written in UTC, as the RFC requires for a rule with a time zone.": "",
  "The times excluded from a series, in the same form as its start.": "",
  "An individually edited occurrence: the time in its series that it replaces (the excluded time closest to it). On import, the series excludes that time and the event references it (`fields.recurrenceId`).": "",
  "Written for every zone used, from the browser's own time zone data (with one rule per year when the changes follow a pattern). On import, a zone that is not an IANA name (such as `W. Europe Standard Time`) follows its VTIMEZONE.": "",
  "On import, a canceled occurrence is excluded from its series, and a canceled event is not added.": "",
  "Printing": "",
  "When printing, every hour, row and column is rendered and visible (a large view is rendered in full for printing), nothing scrolls, colors are preserved, and the toolbar is omitted. A week of the month, a timeline row, a day of the agenda and an appointment are not split across pages.": "",
  "Unit states: the printed appearance, where a design language differs on paper (for example, no card frame).": "",
  "Set on the scheduler while printing. `print()` also marks the page so that only this scheduler prints.": "",
  "`{ range: 'visible' (default) | 'all' | { start, end }, appointments, name }`. Returns the file's text, or `null` if `onICalendarExporting` canceled the export.": "",
  "`{ added, updated, failed }`. Each event is added through the data layer, with `onAppointmentAdding` first. An event whose UID matches an appointment's key updates that appointment.": "",
  "Prints the scheduler alone. Returns `false` if `onPrinting` canceled it.": "",
  "Occurs before writing. Change `appointments` to export different ones.": "",
  "Occurs after writing.": "",
  "Occurs before adding. `appointments` holds the values read, which you can change or filter.": "",
  "Occurs after adding.": "",
  "Occurs before the print dialog opens.": "",
  "Occurs when the print dialog closes, including after the browser's own print command.": "",
  "The iCalendar utilities": "",
  "The reader and writer have no DOM dependency and can be used without a scheduler.": "",
  "Returns the events, time zones and calendar name of a file. It handles folded lines, escaped text, multiple calendars and components inside events, and never throws.": "",
  "Returns the VTIMEZONE of an IANA zone, using `Intl`.": "",
  "Returns the moment a date in a file refers to: in UTC, an IANA zone, the file's VTIMEZONE, or otherwise `fallback`.": ""
}
